{"738090": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "GRIT", "steam_appid": 738090, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/405067dba9f837044f99a987e43f16f7.poster.avif?t=1787086382\" width=1170 height=290 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/405067dba9f837044f99a987e43f16f7.webm?t=1787086382\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/405067dba9f837044f99a987e43f16f7.mp4?t=1787086382\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every gun you pick up in GRIT is also a playing card. Match the suits across your four weapon slots and you stop being one more gunslinger in a duster — you become the Tracker, the Chaplain, the Merchant, or the Cavalry, and most of what you gain, your posse gains with you.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A third-person Wild West battle royale for 100 players. Ride hard, shoot straight, and hold your ground as the Calamity swallows the map.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/9d50ba311ce570b6ac4f0ded8f3c15b5.poster.avif?t=1787086382\" width=1170 height=290 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/9d50ba311ce570b6ac4f0ded8f3c15b5.webm?t=1787086382\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/9d50ba311ce570b6ac4f0ded8f3c15b5.mp4?t=1787086382\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Your Inventory Is Your Hand</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Four weapon slots. Every gun that goes into one carries a rank and suit. The higher the rank, the better the gun.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Get two of the same suit and a perk turns on. Four of the same suit makes you something the rest of the lobby has to plan around.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >So looting a body is a question every time: the better gun, or the one that completes the hand?</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Play the Hand You're Dealt</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Diamonds — The Tracker. </strong>Nobody gets to hide. Put a round in someone and he stays lit up for your whole posse; commit all the way and anyone who shoots at you gives himself away doing it.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hearts — The Chaplain. </strong>Everything that keeps people alive happens quicker around you. Go all in and your remedies carry to whoever's standing close, and the men you revive come back stronger.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Spades — The Merchant. </strong>Armor is a suggestion. Your lead goes through what other men are counting on, and a full hand cuts the whole posse in on the trade.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Clubs — The Cavalry. </strong>The horse isn't how you get to the fight, it's how you win it. Faster, tougher, and eventually something nobody can put down — while you haul teammates back up at a gallop and shoot straighter from the saddle than most men manage on foot.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Duel Your Way Back</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Getting gunned down isn't the end of your match. It's a Second Chance — a 1v1 quick-draw showdown for the right to ride back in.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Win it and you're back in the fight. Lose it and you had your shot.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Second chances are earned on the trigger, not handed out by whoever reaches your body first.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >    <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/31010eb1302b261e2b88ae4603df927a.poster.avif?t=1787086382\" width=1170 height=290 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/31010eb1302b261e2b88ae4603df927a.webm?t=1787086382\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/31010eb1302b261e2b88ae4603df927a.mp4?t=1787086382\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Ride Like You Stole It</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple speeds, shooting on the move, and saddlebags for everything you can't carry yourself.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cut a rival loose from his horse and leave him walking into the storm.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >  <strong>Every Bullet Has to Travel</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Nothing here is hitscan. Lead your target, read the drop, respect the distance.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The long shots you land are yours.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Ride the Rails</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Calamity is the storm that eats the map, and it closes whether you're ready or not.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The train keeps rolling through it. Board it for the loot, stay aboard to hold position inside the ring, and throw off everyone else who had the same idea.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Everyone else is running. You're riding.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/fab6550568c45ffd75d484dac70c06e4.poster.avif?t=1787086382\" width=1170 height=290 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/fab6550568c45ffd75d484dac70c06e4.webm?t=1787086382\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/738090/extras/fab6550568c45ffd75d484dac70c06e4.mp4?t=1787086382\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>No Two Matches Deal the Same Hand</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every match deals three Wildcards off a deck of twenty before a shot is fired.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Calamity might chase the train instead of closing on a circle. Second Chances might be off the table entirely. The Deathcart might be stocked with something it has no business selling.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You find out what you're playing the moment the cards hit the table.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Solo, Duos, and Posses</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >100 players a match, around 25 minutes a round.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Suit perks spill onto your teammates, so a posse that coordinates its hands beats one that doesn't. It's still every posse for itself.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>The CattlePass</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A hundred levels of weapon skins, horse skins, parachutes, outfits, flare, and titles — and the first CattlePass comes with the game.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Eight themed Logbooks with their own missions and rewards, plus a daily Mission for bonus XP.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.stea